<title>GERMANY: DLW sells car components unit to Magna.</title>
<headline>DLW sells car components unit to Magna.</headline>
<dateline>BIETIGHEIM-BISSINGEN, Germany 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German floor covering manufacturer DLW AG said on Wednesday it sold its car components business to Austria's Magna Europa.</p>
<p>DLW said in a mandatory statement it sold 100 percent of its subsidiary Georg Naeher GmbH to Magna but had bought 100 percent of Marka Bodenbelags-Vertriebs-GmbH, a floor coverings distributor belonging to Naeher.</p>
<p>Magna Europa bought Naeher with backdated effect from January 1, 1997 and the contracts were signed on April 22. The purchase by DLW of Marka Bodenbelags-Vertriebs-GmbH also takes backdated effect from January 1.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
